From: cjom <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: request the HW render context on every game load

libretro.h documents RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_HW_RENDER as "Should be called
in retro_load_game()". setup_hw_rendering(), which issues it, was only
called from retro_init() -- once per process -- and from
update_variables() when the HW-mode option changes.

A frontend that unloads and reloads the shared object per game re-runs
retro_init() every time, so it never noticed. A frontend that keeps the
core loaded gets no HW render request for the second game: it never calls
context_reset, the OpenGL graphics manager finds no current context, and
gladLoad*() returns 0:

  Couldn't initialize OpenGL          (graphics/opengl/context.cpp)

That is a fatal error(), so the core aborts and the frontend drops back to
its own UI. The first game of a session runs and every one after it fails.

Request it in retro_load_game() as documented. The retro_init() call is
left in place so first-load behaviour, including the pixel format it sets,
is unchanged.

diff --git a/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp b/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp
index e3bb35a..3c1ff08 100644
--- a/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp
+++ b/backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-core.cpp
@@ -1088,6 +1088,22 @@ bool retro_load_game(const struct retro_game_info *game) {
 		game_buf_ptr = NULL;
 	}
 
+	/* Re-request the hardware render context for this game. libretro.h says of
+	   RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_HW_RENDER: "Should be called in retro_load_game()",
+	   but the only calls were retro_init() -- once per process -- and
+	   update_variables() when the HW mode option changes.
+
+	   A frontend that unloads the core between games re-runs retro_init() and so
+	   never noticed. One that keeps it loaded gets no HW render request for the
+	   second game, never calls context_reset, and the OpenGL graphics manager
+	   then finds no current context:
+
+	     Couldn't initialize OpenGL          (graphics/opengl/context.cpp)
+
+	   which is a fatal error(), so the core aborts and the frontend is left
+	   dropping back to its own UI. */
+	setup_hw_rendering();
+
 	if (!retro_init_emu_thread()) {
 		if (retro_log_cb)
 			retro_log_cb(RETRO_LOG_ERROR, "[scummvm] Failed to initialize emulation thread!\n");
